---
// THE CALCULATOR WIZARD.
//
// THE CENTRAL FACT, worth restating here: the honest calc engine (src/scripts/calc-engine.js)
// already exists and does all the math. This component is a front end that feeds it, one
// question at a time. It does not compute anything itself.
//
// HOW IT STAYS HONEST TO THE ENGINE'S DOM CONTRACT. render() reaches for about 45 element
// ids, most without a null check, and it does not care whether a page shows them through a
// step-by-step wizard or all at once like the inline calculator. So this component renders a
// full, real copy of the estimator inputs (room, flight, travelers, nights, style) plus the
// existing <CalcResult>, exactly like CountryBriefing.astro does, and keeps them in the DOM the
// whole time. They are not hidden with the `hidden` attribute (the engine already manages that
// on #hn-app itself); instead a wrapper div is visually collapsed by this component's own CSS
// until the wizard finishes, then revealed. The engine never knows a wizard is involved: it
// just sees its inputs change and its outputs get read, exactly as it does on a country guide.
//
// UX REWORK (see BRIEF-calculator-ux-rework.md). This pass changes the LOOK and FLOW only:
// a dark focus frame around the whole flow, destination shown as a completed step 1 with a
// change link, real preset-plus-stepper controls for travelers and nights, a typed-price
// control for flight and hotel, and bigger tap targets throughout. None of that touches
// calc-engine.js, avoidable.js or calc-lines.js, and the estimator markup below (ids, classes,
// structure) is byte-for-byte what it was before this pass. Handoff notes on the two items in
// the brief this file could not act on:
//   - Point 8, "the mislabeled 'where are you staying' = restaurant meal dropdown": no such
//     mislabeling exists in this snapshot. #hnRegionWrap / #hnRegion is a real, correctly
//     labeled engine control for countries whose tourist tax varies by region, and it is
//     already hidden unless calc-engine.js finds more than one region for this country. It is
//     a live input the engine writes into without a null check (see calc-engine.js around
//     `regionWrap`/`regionSel`), so removing it would break the DOM contract for any
//     multi-region country. Left exactly as it was. Flagged to MAIN in the handoff.
//   - Part B's "book direct on lodging" / "skip an unneeded eSIM" named-tactic examples do not
//     exist as avoidable.js items in this snapshot (avoidable.js's items are: paying in
//     dollars/DCC, the bank's own fees, the exchange desk, a VAT/GST refund, the free arrival
//     form scammed by lookalikes, a reseller markup, a dead product, double-tipping a service
//     charge, and a claimable exemption). The wording guard on a lodging/OTA tactic therefore
//     has nothing to attach to without adding a new avoidable.js item, which is out of scope
//     here (avoidable.js is on the do-not-touch list). Flagged to MAIN.
//
// THE STEP LIST IS DATA (see the client script below), not hardcoded screens, so a future
// honest addition (a season-tier context line, a connectivity verdict, anything that adds
// judgment rather than a price) is one more entry in that array, wired the same way. Adding a
// step must never mean restructuring this shell. Each step now carries a `type`
// ('stepperPreset', 'price' or 'choice') that decides which control the shell renders, on top
// of the same `apply()` wiring into the real, hidden estimator inputs.
//
// THE SEVEN QUESTIONS. Destination is step 1, already answered by however the reader got to
// this country's URL (the /calculator index, an on-ramp link, or typing it directly), so this
// component's own step list starts at step 2 and runs to step 7: travelers, nights, travel
// style, flight price, hotel price, card type. Three questions from the original brief (cash
// percentage, ATM frequency, travel month) were dropped rather than asked and ignored: the
// engine derives cash and ATM behaviour from travel style automatically, and travel month
// moves nothing in an honest model (see calc-lines.js: "we publish no seasonal uplift because
// an honest one does not exist"). Asking a question that visibly does nothing is exactly the
// theatre this wizard exists to avoid. This pass renders destination itself as a completed,
// changeable step 1 inside the shell, so the numbering the reader sees now covers the whole
// sequence, not just the six live questions.
import CalcResult from './CalcResult.astro';
import { calcSetupFor } from '../data/calc-setup.js';

const { country: c } = Astro.props;
const { calcJson, tipCalc } = calcSetupFor(c);
const styles = (c.cash && c.cash.styles) || [];
const defaultStyleIndex = (c.cash && c.cash.defaultIndex) || 0;

// Flight and hotel preset amounts for the wizard's tappable options. Flight uses this
// country's own verified round-trip range where one exists (the same figure the inline
// calculator prefills), never an invented one; hotel uses the travel style's own typical
// room price. Both stay fully editable inside the estimator once the wizard hands off.
const flightData = c.flight || null;
const flightTypical = flightData ? Math.round((flightData.low + flightData.high) / 2 / 10) * 10 : 700;
const roomTypical = (styles[defaultStyleIndex] && styles[defaultStyleIndex].room) || 150;

// Handed to the client script as inert JSON, the same pattern #hn-data already uses.
const wizData = {
  countryName: c.name,
  styles: styles.map((s, i) => ({ i, n: s.n, room: s.room })),
  defaultStyleIndex,
  flightTypical,
  roomTypical,
};
const wizJson = JSON.stringify(wizData).replace(/</g, "\\u003c");
---
<div class="wiz-focus">
  <div class="wiz-wrap">

    {/* ================= THE WIZARD SHELL, one question at a time =================
        The completed "step 1: destination" strip renders once, inside the same card, above
        whichever question is live; the client script only ever rewrites #wizQuestion. */}
    <div class="wiz" id="wizShell" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="wiz-dest" id="wizDest">
        <span class="wiz-dest-check" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="wiz-dest-label">Step 1 &middot; Destination</span>
        <span class="wiz-dest-name">{c.name}</span>
        <a class="wiz-dest-change" href="/calculator">Change</a>
      </div>
      <div id="wizQuestion"></div>
    </div>

    {/* ================= THE REAL ENGINE, visually collapsed until the wizard hands off =================
        Same estimator inputs and the same <CalcResult> the inline per-country calculator uses,
        same ids, so calc-engine.js finds everything it expects. Nothing here is a second copy of
        the math: it is the actual inputs, driven by the wizard's answers instead of by hand. */}
    <div class="wiz-underlay" id="wizUnderlay" hidden>
      <!-- Everything the engine needs, handed over as inert JSON. No card data ships. -->
      <script type="application/json" id="hn-data" set:html={calcJson}></script>
      <script type="application/json" id="wiz-data" set:html={wizJson}></script>

      <div class="estimator" id="hn-app" hidden>
        <div class="erow">
          <div class="ef ef-room">
            <label for="hnRoom">Hotel price a night</label>
            <span class="moneyin"><span class="mny">$</span><input id="hnRoom" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="150" aria-label="Hotel price per night in US dollars" /></span>
          </div>
          <label class="hn-toggle hn-toggle-inline" id="hnPaidWrap">
            <input type="checkbox" id="hnPaid" />
            <span class="hn-switch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="hn-toggle-l">Already paid for the room</span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <p class="ef-hint-room" id="hnRoomHint" hidden></p>

        <label class="cf hn-region" id="hnRegionWrap" hidden style="display:none">
          <span class="cf-l">Where are you staying?</span>
          <span class="selwrap"><select id="hnRegion"></select></span>
        </label>

        <div class="erow erow-flight">
          <div class="ef ef-flight">
            <label for="hnFlight">Flights, round trip a person</label>
            <span class="moneyin"><span class="mny">$</span><input id="hnFlight" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="" aria-label="Round trip flight price per traveler in US dollars" /></span>
          </div>
          <p class="ef-hint" id="hnFlightHint">Optional. Enter your round trip fare per traveler to fold flights into the total.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="erow">
          <div class="ef ef-num"><label>Travelers</label>
            <span class="stepper">
              <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnTrav" data-dir="-1" aria-label="One fewer traveler">&#8722;</button>
              <span class="stp-v" id="hnTrav" data-v="2">2</span>
              <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnTrav" data-dir="1" aria-label="One more traveler">+</button>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="ef ef-num"><label>Nights</label>
            <span class="stepper">
              <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnNights" data-dir="-1" aria-label="One fewer night">&#8722;</button>
              <span class="stp-v" id="hnNights" data-v="7">7</span>
              <button type="button" class="stp" data-step="hnNights" data-dir="1" aria-label="One more night">+</button>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="ef ef-style"><label>Style</label>
            <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Travel style">
              {styles.map((s, i) => (
                <button id={"hnStyle" + i} class={i === defaultStyleIndex ? "on" : ""} type="button" data-per={s.per} data-cash={s.cash} data-room={s.room}>{s.n}</button>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <CalcResult country={c} tipCalc={tipCalc} hideWizardCta={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  // The wizard's own driver. It writes into the real inputs above and fires native events on
  // them, exactly the events their own listeners (inside calc-engine.js) already expect. It
  // never touches render() directly and never recomputes a total itself.
  (function () {
    const shell = document.getElementById('wizShell');
    const destBar = document.getElementById('wizDest');
    const question = document.getElementById('wizQuestion');
    const underlay = document.getElementById('wizUnderlay');
    const wdEl = document.getElementById('wiz-data');
    if (!shell || !destBar || !question || !underlay || !wdEl) return;

    let WD;
    try { WD = JSON.parse(wdEl.textContent); } catch (e) { return; }

    const id = (x) => document.getElementById(x);
    const fire = (el, type) => el.dispatchEvent(new Event(type, { bubbles: true }));
    const usd = (v) => '$' + Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-US');

    // ----- one wiring function per real engine input the wizard can set -----
    function setStepper(key, target) {
      const el = id(key);
      if (!el) return;
      let guard = 0;
      while (+el.dataset.v !== target && guard < 80) {
        const dir = target > +el.dataset.v ? '1' : '-1';
        const btn = document.querySelector('.stp[data-step="' + key + '"][data-dir="' + dir + '"]');
        if (!btn || btn.disabled) break;
        fire(btn, 'click');
        guard++;
      }
    }
    function setMoneyInput(key, value) {
      const el = id(key);
      if (!el) return;
      el.value = String(Math.round(value));
      fire(el, 'input');
    }
    function clickStyle(i) {
      const btn = id('hnStyle' + i);
      if (btn) fire(btn, 'click');
    }
    function setNoFee(on) {
      const el = id('hnNoFee');
      if (!el) return;
      el.checked = on;
      fire(el, 'change');
    }

    // ----- THE STEP LIST, as data. A future honest addition is one more entry here, wired
    // the same way; the shell below never needs to change to add one. `type` picks the
    // control: 'stepperPreset' (presets plus a live +/- stepper, requires Continue),
    // 'price' (a typed dollar figure prefilled with a typical, requires Continue), or
    // 'choice' (tappable chips that advance immediately, the old behaviour). -----
    const STEPS = [
      {
        id: 'travelers',
        overall: 2,
        type: 'stepperPreset',
        label: 'Travelers',
        question: 'How many travelers?',
        helper: 'Changes the per-person entry charges and the daily spend.',
        typical: 2,
        min: 1,
        max: 12, // matches calc-engine.js's own hnTrav limit, so the wizard never asks for
                 // a value the real stepper would refuse.
        presets: [1, 2, 3, 4],
        apply(v) { setStepper('hnTrav', v); },
      },
      {
        id: 'nights',
        overall: 3,
        type: 'stepperPreset',
        label: 'Nights',
        question: 'How many nights?',
        helper: 'The room total and the tourist tax both scale with this.',
        typical: 7,
        min: 1,
        max: 60, // matches calc-engine.js's own hnNights limit.
        presets: [5, 7, 14, 21],
        apply(v) { setStepper('hnNights', v); },
      },
      {
        id: 'style',
        overall: 4,
        type: 'choice',
        label: 'Travel style',
        question: 'What is your travel style?',
        helper: 'Sets a typical daily spend and room price. Edit either later.',
        typical: WD.defaultStyleIndex,
        options: WD.styles.map((s) => ({ label: s.n, value: s.i })),
        apply(v) { clickStyle(v); },
      },
      {
        id: 'flight',
        overall: 5,
        type: 'price',
        label: 'Flights',
        question: 'About how much is your round trip flight, per person?',
        helper: 'Paid in dollars at booking, so it carries no foreign fee.',
        typical: WD.flightTypical,
        apply(v) { setMoneyInput('hnFlight', v); },
      },
      {
        id: 'hotel',
        overall: 6,
        type: 'price',
        label: 'Hotel',
        question: 'About how much is your hotel, per night?',
        helper: 'Fully editable once you reach the total below.',
        typical: WD.roomTypical,
        apply(v) { setMoneyInput('hnRoom', v); },
      },
      {
        id: 'card',
        overall: 7,
        type: 'choice',
        label: 'Your card',
        question: 'What kind of card are you bringing?',
        helper: 'Most US cards charge a foreign fee without saying so.',
        typical: 'regular',
        options: [
          { label: 'A regular card (most US cards add about a 3% foreign fee)', value: 'regular' },
          { label: 'A no-foreign-fee card', value: 'nofee' },
        ],
        apply(v) { setNoFee(v === 'nofee'); },
      },
    ];
    const TOTAL_STEPS = 7; // destination (step 1, shown as the completed strip above) plus
                            // the six live questions below.

    let stepIndex = 0;
    const answers = {};

    function esc(s) {
      return String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[c]));
    }

    function chosenFor(s) {
      return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(answers, s.id) ? answers[s.id] : s.typical;
    }

    function progressHtml(s) {
      const pct = Math.round((s.overall / TOTAL_STEPS) * 100);
      return '<div class="wiz-progress"><div class="wiz-bar"><div class="wiz-bar-fill" style="width:' + pct + '%"></div></div>' +
        '<span class="wiz-step-n">Step ' + s.overall + ' of ' + TOTAL_STEPS + '</span></div>';
    }

    function navHtml(showContinue) {
      return '<div class="wiz-nav">' +
        (stepIndex > 0 ? '<button type="button" class="wiz-back">&#8592; Back</button>' : '<span></span>') +
        (showContinue ? '<button type="button" class="wiz-continue">Continue &#8594;</button>' : '<span></span>') +
        '</div>';
    }

    function renderStep() {
      const s = STEPS[stepIndex];
      if (s.type === 'stepperPreset') renderStepperPreset(s);
      else if (s.type === 'price') renderPrice(s);
      else renderChoice(s);
    }

    // ----- 'choice': tappable chips, advances on tap, exactly like before. -----
    function renderChoice(s) {
      const chosen = chosenFor(s);
      question.innerHTML =
        progressHtml(s) +
        '<p class="wiz-label">' + esc(s.label) + '</p>' +
        '<h2 class="wiz-q">' + esc(s.question) + '</h2>' +
        (s.helper ? '<p class="wiz-helper">' + esc(s.helper) + '</p>' : '') +
        '<div class="wiz-opts" role="group" aria-label="' + esc(s.question) + '">' +
        s.options.map((o) => (
          '<button type="button" class="wiz-opt' + (o.value === chosen ? ' wiz-opt-on' : '') + '" data-value="' + esc(String(o.value)) + '">' + esc(o.label) + (o.value === s.typical ? '<span class="wiz-typ">typical</span>' : '') + '</button>'
        )).join('') +
        '</div>' +
        navHtml(false);

      question.querySelectorAll('.wiz-opt').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const raw = btn.dataset.value;
          const v = s.options.find((o) => String(o.value) === raw).value;
          choose(s, v, true);
        });
      });
      wireNav();
    }

    // ----- 'stepperPreset': preset chips plus a real +/- stepper. Presets set the value on
    // one tap; the stepper is the fine-tune, so there is no separate "enter my own" control
    // and no "not sure" skip text, the pre-highlighted typical preset already covers that. -----
    function renderStepperPreset(s) {
      const chosen = Number(chosenFor(s));
      question.innerHTML =
        progressHtml(s) +
        '<p class="wiz-label">' + esc(s.label) + '</p>' +
        '<h2 class="wiz-q">' + esc(s.question) + '</h2>' +
        (s.helper ? '<p class="wiz-helper">' + esc(s.helper) + '</p>' : '') +
        '<div class="wiz-stp-row">' +
        '<button type="button" class="wiz-stp-btn" data-dir="-1" aria-label="Decrease" ' + (chosen <= s.min ? 'disabled' : '') + '>&#8722;</button>' +
        '<span class="wiz-stp-val" aria-live="polite">' + chosen + '</span>' +
        '<button type="button" class="wiz-stp-btn" data-dir="1" aria-label="Increase" ' + (chosen >= s.max ? 'disabled' : '') + '>+</button>' +
        '</div>' +
        '<div class="wiz-presets" role="group" aria-label="Quick pick">' +
        s.presets.map((p) => (
          '<button type="button" class="wiz-preset' + (p === chosen ? ' wiz-preset-on' : '') + '" data-value="' + p + '">' + p + (p === s.typical ? '<span class="wiz-typ">typical</span>' : '') + '</button>'
        )).join('') +
        '</div>' +
        navHtml(true);

      question.querySelectorAll('.wiz-preset').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const v = +btn.dataset.value;
          setValue(s, v);
        });
      });
      question.querySelectorAll('.wiz-stp-btn').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const dir = +btn.dataset.dir;
          const next = Math.min(s.max, Math.max(s.min, chosen + dir));
          setValue(s, next);
        });
      });
      wireNav();
    }

    // ----- 'price': a typed dollar figure, prefilled with a typical, no invented presets. -----
    function renderPrice(s) {
      const chosen = Math.round(Number(chosenFor(s)));
      question.innerHTML =
        progressHtml(s) +
        '<p class="wiz-label">' + esc(s.label) + '</p>' +
        '<h2 class="wiz-q">' + esc(s.question) + '</h2>' +
        (s.helper ? '<p class="wiz-helper">' + esc(s.helper) + '</p>' : '') +
        '<div class="wiz-price-row">' +
        '<span class="wiz-price-dollar" aria-hidden="true">$</span>' +
        '<input class="wiz-price-input" id="wizPriceInput" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="' + chosen + '" aria-label="' + esc(s.question) + '">' +
        '</div>' +
        '<p class="wiz-price-hint">This is a typical figure for ' + esc(WD.countryName) + '. Know yours? Type it in.</p>' +
        navHtml(true);

      const inputEl = question.querySelector('#wizPriceInput');
      if (inputEl) {
        inputEl.addEventListener('input', () => {
          const v = Math.max(0, parseInt(inputEl.value.replace(/[^0-9]/g, ''), 10) || 0);
          answers[s.id] = v;
          s.apply(v);
        });
        // Focusing and selecting on tap is what makes "type it in" actually easy on mobile,
        // since the field starts full of the typical figure rather than empty.
        inputEl.addEventListener('focus', () => inputEl.select());
      }
      wireNav();
    }

    function setValue(s, v) {
      answers[s.id] = v;
      s.apply(v);
      renderStep();
    }

    function wireNav() {
      const backBtn = question.querySelector('.wiz-back');
      if (backBtn) backBtn.addEventListener('click', goBack);
      const contBtn = question.querySelector('.wiz-continue');
      if (contBtn) contBtn.addEventListener('click', () => advance());
    }

    // choose(): used by 'choice' steps, which both record the answer and move on in one tap.
    function choose(s, value, advanceNow) {
      answers[s.id] = value;
      s.apply(value);
      if (advanceNow) advance();
      else renderStep();
    }

    function advance() {
      if (stepIndex < STEPS.length - 1) {
        stepIndex++;
        renderStep();
      } else {
        finish();
      }
    }

    function goBack() {
      if (stepIndex > 0) {
        stepIndex--;
        renderStep();
      }
    }

    function finish() {
      shell.hidden = true;
      underlay.hidden = false;
      if (typeof underlay.scrollIntoView === 'function') {
        try { underlay.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }
        catch (e) { try { underlay.scrollIntoView(); } catch (e2) { /* no-op: nothing sensible left to try */ } }
      }
    }

    // The result view's own "Change answers" button (see CalcResult.astro) dispatches this
    // rather than reaching into this closure directly, so the two components stay decoupled:
    // CalcResult knows nothing about the wizard's internals, only that this event exists.
    window.addEventListener('ttc-wizard-change-answers', () => {
      underlay.hidden = true;
      shell.hidden = false;
      renderStep();
      if (typeof shell.scrollIntoView === 'function') {
        try { shell.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }
        catch (e) { try { shell.scrollIntoView(); } catch (e2) { /* no-op */ } }
      }
    });

    renderStep();
  })();
</script>

<script>
  // The calculator engine, shared with the inline per-country calculator. Imported for its
  // side effects: it hydrates from #hn-data and #hn-app the moment both exist, which they do
  // above, kept visually collapsed until the wizard finishes.
  import '../scripts/calc-engine.js';
</script>

<style>
  /* ===== PART A, POINT 1: FULL FOCUS =====
     Once the reader is in the calculator it is the only thing on screen: a dark frame lifts
     the white wizard card off the page, and nothing from the surrounding layout competes
     around it. The frame wraps both the question shell and the handed-off estimator/result,
     so the focus treatment holds through the whole flow, not just the Q&A part of it. */
  .wiz-focus{background:#0E3B31;border-radius:20px;padding:28px 16px;margin:0 0 8px}
  .wiz-wrap{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto}

  /* ----- the wizard shell ----- */
  .wiz{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);box-shadow:0 18px 40px -14px rgba(0,0,0,.45);padding:24px 26px 26px}

  /* Destination, shown as a completed, changeable step 1 above whichever question is live. */
  .wiz-dest{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;padding:0 0 16px;margin:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);flex-wrap:wrap}
  .wiz-dest-check{flex:none;width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--green-bg);color:#10502C;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
  .wiz-dest-label{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}
  .wiz-dest-name{font-size:14.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);margin-right:auto}
  .wiz-dest-change{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal-deep);text-decoration:none;padding:4px 2px}
  .wiz-dest-change:hover{text-decoration:underline}

  .wiz-progress{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;margin:0 0 20px}
  .wiz-bar{height:6px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--line);overflow:hidden}
  .wiz-bar-fill{height:100%;background:var(--teal);border-radius:999px;transition:width .3s ease}
  .wiz-step-n{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}
  .wiz-label{margin:0 0 6px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--teal-deep)}
